tvBro is a media player only. It ships no channels, streams, playlists or other content and is not
affiliated with any content provider. Users add their own sources and are responsible for having the
rights to them.

This product includes software developed by third parties, each under its own license; the full
list with versions is in docs/THIRD_PARTY.md. In short:

Android app:
- AndroidX (Jetpack Compose, Activity, Lifecycle, Core, Work, Room, Security-crypto, ProfileInstaller,
  Media3 ExoPlayer / HLS / UI / OkHttp datasource), Google Tink, Guava, Gson: Apache-2.0
- Kotlin stdlib, kotlinx.coroutines, kotlinx.serialization, kotlinx-datetime: Apache-2.0
- OkHttp / Okio (Square): Apache-2.0
- ZXing core (QR code encoder): Apache-2.0
- jcifs-ng (SMB/CIFS client for recording to a network share): LGPL-2.1, used unmodified as a separate
  library; source https://github.com/AgNO3/jcifs-ng. With it: Bouncy Castle (MIT-style), SLF4J API (MIT)

Desktop app (Windows x64, Linux arm64):
- JetBrains Compose Multiplatform for Desktop, Skiko: Apache-2.0; Skia: BSD-3-Clause
- JNA / JNA Platform: Apache-2.0 (dual-licensed with LGPL-2.1)
- kXML2: BSD-style; sqlite-jdbc: Apache-2.0 (SQLite: public domain)
- Bundled Java runtime (Eclipse Temurin OpenJDK 17): GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception,
  source https://github.com/adoptium/jdk17u
- libmpv (video engine) is loaded at run time as a separate shared library and is not part of the
  tvBro distribution: on Linux the system package (libmpv2), on Windows a libmpv-2.dll the user
  installs (see docs/INSTALL.md). mpv: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv

Web app:
- cryptography (Python): Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause
- hls.js, mpegts.js (fetched at deploy time): Apache-2.0
- FFmpeg is run as an external program installed by the operator; it is not distributed with tvBro.
